\begin_inset Formula $P_k\cdot A$
\end_inset
; interpolatory weights through the 
\begin_inset Formula $n+1$
\end_inset
 samples would be exact only for 
\begin_inset Formula $A$
\end_inset
 of degree 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset
, which is not enough for 
\begin_inset Formula $g_1$
\end_inset
 when 
\begin_inset Formula $n\ge3$
\end_inset
. For orders 2 and 4 the rule coincides with the Newton-Cotes rule (nodes 
\begin_inset Formula $\pm1$
\end_inset
, and 
\begin_inset Formula $-1,0,1$
